{"name":"README","kind":"note","text":"The behaviour contract of the SOFT router, one case per line. The router reads ONE line out of a spawn prompt -- `KIND: <name>` -- resolves that kind's ladder and rewrites model, subagent_type and a header. It never denies a spawn for a routing reason, never guesses a kind from topic words or path globs, and never applies a default to a spawn that named nothing. The only denials in this file are the call cap's. Schema: {name, matrix_fixture, router_config?, hook_stdin, precondition?, projects_fixture?, expected}. matrix_fixture is \"live\" (the fixture guide, tests/router/fixtures/matrix.md) or {replace:[[regex,replacement],...]} applied line-wise to it, or {literal:\"...\"}. router_config is the [router] table of the one optional config file; absent means the code defaults. precondition.write_marker arms a cooldown marker at a given age; precondition.write_agent drops a generated agent file in $AGENTS_DIR. projects_fixture materialises one CLI subagent transcript: {agent_id, calls, lane_dir}. $CWD, $AGENTS_DIR and $TMP expand to the tmp world. decision is allow|deny; model/subagent_type null means the field is absent from updatedInput (the spawn went through UNTOUCHED, which is the soft router's default)."}
